informal_statement:
For integers $n$, let \[f(n) = \left\{
\begin{array}{cl}
n^2 & \text{ if }n\text{ is odd}, \\
n^2 - 4n - 1 & \text{ if }n\text{ is even}.
\end{array}
\right.\]Find $f(f(f(f(f(4)))))$. Show that it is 1.

Let \[f(x) = \begin{cases}
-x^2 - 1 &\text{if }x<0, \\
2&\text{if }0 \le x< 4, \\
\sqrt{x}&\text{if }x \ge 4.
\end{cases}
\]Find $f(\pi)$. Show that it is 2.
